output:
 {
  "review": "No, this has nothing to do with the sitcom 'Seinfeld' or its eccentric and hilarious character Cosmo Kramer. In reality, 'Kramer vs. Kramer' is a fine drama movie, without a doubt one of the finest of its kind and one of the greatest movies ever. I'm glad that it won more Oscars than 'Apocalypse Now' because it really deserved such glory.<br /><br />'Kramer vs. Kramer' is an excellent film, so well made and so perfectly balanced that I wouldn't change anything about it in any way. There is nothing wrong with the film. It's film-making of the highest quality. And it stands the test of time, too. Not only it doesn't look any dated, but also its cultural impact is long-lasting and its realistic story remains just as significant as it was when it came out in 1979. A timeless classic. They don't make movies like this today.<br /><br />This movie is dramatic, realistic, simple but brilliant, intense, powerful, sweet and even tragic and depressing sometimes. Yet, it has fine humor as well. It has no special effects, but who cares? This is not the movie or place to discuss such thing. For a movie like this, such thing would be pointless and absolutely unnecessary.<br /><br />The story is very interesting. The actors's chemistry is just perfect. All of the actors are great, but the 3 main ones are the very best. Dustin Hoffman, a brilliant actor, has his greatest performance ever here as the lovable but distant workaholic Ted Kramer. Meryl Streep is great as Ted's wife, Joanna. And cute little Justin Henry is terrific as the loving but sometimes stubborn Billy, son of Ted and Joanna.<br /><br />The soundtrack is all instrumental and wonderful. The opening song (by the guitarist Frederic Hand) is brilliant. The rest of the soundtrack is mostly Antonio Vivaldi's classical music and is simply dazzling.<br /><br />This motion picture has also an incredible development of the characters. See the character Ted Kramer: a workaholic who becomes an amazing father after being left with no choice but to take care of his son, trying to adjust these new responsibilities with his job after being left by his wife Joanna. With this, Ted learns about the most beautiful things in life, but also realizes how though life is, with the problems in his job and the return of Joanna, who wants the custody of their son. But even Joanna changes for better and the ending is an unexpected surprise when one sees this for the first time.<br /><br />This movie has also some thoughtful things, such as courtroom scenes where both Ted and Joanna face brutal character assassinations unleashed by the lawyers. Another thoughtful thing to see is when poor Billy falls off a jungle gym with his toy (a plane) and gets seriously injured on his face. But then again, the scene is very well made and what comes next is very intense: his father runs quickly and crosses numerous blocks, ignoring the traffic to take his son to the hospital.<br /><br />Overall, this is a movie which is a good lesson of life.<br /><br />This should definitely be on Top 250.",
  "translate": "{   \"recensione\": \"No, questo non ha niente a che fare con la sitcom 'Seinfeld' o il suo personaggio eccentrico e hilarante Cosmo Kramer. In realtà, 'Kramer vs. Kramer' è un film drammatico di alto livello, senza dubbio uno dei più fini del suo genere e uno dei migliori film mai realizzati.<br /><br />'Kramer vs. Kramer' è un film eccellente, così ben fatto e perfettamente bilanciato che non cambierebbe nulla di esso in alcun modo. C'è qualcosa sbagliato con il film. È una direzione alta della migliore qualità. E resiste al tempo, anche.<br /><br />Non solo non ha un aspetto datato, ma anche l'impatto culturale è duraturo e la sua storia realistica rimane sempre significativa come era quando è stato pubblicato per la prima volta nel 1979. Un classico in tempo.<br /><br />Non si fa più dei film come questi oggi.<br /><br />Questo film è drammatico, realistico, semplicemente geniale, intensivo, potente, dolce e anche triste e depressante a volte. Ma ha anche buon umorismo.<br /><br />Non ha effetti speciali, ma chi se ne preoccupa? Questo non è il film o il posto per discutere di tale cosa. Per un film come questo, ciò sarebbe inutile e del tutto inutile.<br /><br />La storia è molto interessante. La chimica degli attori è perfetta. Tutti gli attori sono grandi, ma i 3 principali sono i migliori.<br /><br />Dustin Hoffman, un attore brillante, ha la sua prestazione più grande qui come il carino ma distanziato lavoraholic Ted Kramer. Meryl Streep è grande come la moglie di Ted, Joanna. E il piccolo Justin Henry è terribile come il figlio amorevole ma occasionalmente scomodo Billy, figlio di Ted e Joanna.<br /><br />La colonna sonora è interamente strumentale e meravigliosa. La canzone d'apertura (del chitarrista Frederic Hand) è brillante.<br /><br />Questo film ha anche un sviluppo incisivo dei personaggi.<br /><br />Guardare il personaggio Ted Kramer: un lavoraholic che diventa un padre eccellente dopo aver ricevuto poca scelta tranne quella di prendersi cura del figlio, cercando di adattarsi a queste nuove responsabilità con il suo lavoro dopo essere stato lasciato dalla moglie Joanna. Con questo, Ted impara le cose più belle della vita, ma anche capisce che la vita è difficile, con i problemi nel suo lavoro e il ritorno di Joanna, che vuole la tutela del figlio.<br /><br />Ancora un aspetto interessante da vedere è quando il povero Billy cade dalla giungla gym con il suo giocattolo (un aereo) e subisce gravi ferite al volto.<br /><br />Ma poi ancora, la scena è molto bene fatta e ciò che segue è molto intensivo: il padre corre rapidamente attraverso i numerosi blocchi, ignora il traffico per portare il figlio all'ospedale.<br /><br />In generale, questo è un film che è una buona lezione sulla vita.<br /><br />Questo dovrebbe essere a Top 250.",
  "language": "italian"
}

json_output:
{
  "review": "No, this has nothing to do with the sitcom 'Seinfeld' or its eccentric and hilarious character Cosmo Kramer. In reality, 'Kramer vs. Kramer' is a fine drama movie, without a doubt one of the finest of its kind and one of the greatest movies ever. I'm glad that it won more Oscars than 'Apocalypse Now' because it really deserved such glory.<br /><br />'Kramer vs. Kramer' is an excellent film, so well made and so perfectly balanced that I wouldn't change anything about it in any way. There is nothing wrong with the film. It's film-making of the highest quality. And it stands the test of time, too. Not only it doesn't look any dated, but also its cultural impact is long-lasting and its realistic story remains just as significant as it was when it came out in 1979. A timeless classic. They don't make movies like this today.<br /><br />This movie is dramatic, realistic, simple but brilliant, intense, powerful, sweet and even tragic and depressing sometimes. Yet, it has fine humor as well. It has no special effects, but who cares? This is not the movie or place to discuss such thing. For a movie like this, such thing would be pointless and absolutely unnecessary.<br /><br />The story is very interesting. The actors's chemistry is just perfect. All of the actors are great, but the 3 main ones are the very best. Dustin Hoffman, a brilliant actor, has his greatest performance ever here as the lovable but distant workaholic Ted Kramer. Meryl Streep is great as Ted's wife, Joanna. And cute little Justin Henry is terrific as the loving but sometimes stubborn Billy, son of Ted and Joanna.<br /><br />The soundtrack is all instrumental and wonderful. The opening song (by the guitarist Frederic Hand) is brilliant. The rest of the soundtrack is mostly Antonio Vivaldi's classical music and is simply dazzling.<br /><br />This motion picture has also an incredible development of the characters. See the character Ted Kramer: a workaholic who becomes an amazing father after being left with no choice but to take care of his son, trying to adjust these new responsibilities with his job after being left by his wife Joanna. With this, Ted learns about the most beautiful things in life, but also realizes how though life is, with the problems in his job and the return of Joanna, who wants the custody of their son. But even Joanna changes for better and the ending is an unexpected surprise when one sees this for the first time.<br /><br />This movie has also some thoughtful things, such as courtroom scenes where both Ted and Joanna face brutal character assassinations unleashed by the lawyers. Another thoughtful thing to see is when poor Billy falls off a jungle gym with his toy (a plane) and gets seriously injured on his face. But then again, the scene is very well made and what comes next is very intense: his father runs quickly and crosses numerous blocks, ignoring the traffic to take his son to the hospital.<br /><br />Overall, this is a movie which is a good lesson of life.<br /><br />This should definitely be on Top 250.",
